# Alice's IAM Policy (Account A — 111111111111) — HAS the allow

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::shared-data",
        "arn:aws:s3:::shared-data/*"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

# Bucket Policy (Account B — 222222222222) — does NOT grant Account A

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "AllowInternalTeam",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::222222222222:role/internal-reader"
      },
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::shared-data/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

Note: Alice's IAM policy already allows `s3:GetObject`, but the bucket policy on
account 222222222222 only names an in-account role; it never grants account A
(111111111111) or Alice's principal. The resource-side link of the cross-account
chain is missing.
